 Off by default: each controller is a player as soon as it connects, in the order the system lists them. On: a controller becomes a player only when you press one of its buttons, as the lowest player free, so the players choose their order and how many play. That press also reaches the game. When a game asks for more players than have joined, a prompt over the game waits for the others to press a button; B closes it.
 
+### Phone controllers
+
+Mac only, off by default. On, the app listens on this Mac for controller input sent by a phone or another program and gives each sender a player of its own, like a controller ([Network pads](mac-controllers.md#network-pads-phones-and-other-programs)). It listens on `127.0.0.1` only, so nothing outside this Mac can reach it, but any program on this Mac can send input to it while it is on. It needs a sender: the app does not include one. Rumble and motion are not sent to the phone.
+
